{
  "_comment": "NonParallel merch, made by the Printify workflow (scripts/printify-sync.mjs). `designs` are the artwork (8000px PNGs in Printify's uploads; `url` is a public PNG Printify fetches once, found again by `fileName`). Each of `lines` is one blank (tee, hoodie, sticker, mug…) made in each of its `designs`, on the colors in `designColors` (or `colors`). A blank is `blueprintId` or `find` (regexes tried in order against Printify's \"brand model title\"); without `printProviders` any US printer with those colors is used. `placements` are Printify print-area coordinates (x, y = centre, scale = width of the 8000px design canvas relative to the print area; the art fills ~80% of the canvas width and ~60% of its height). Every price is what Printify charges us (the item plus US shipping) plus `markup` (0.2 = 20%), with Stripe's 2.9% + 30¢ on top so the 20% is what we keep, rounded up to a tidy price ending in 5 or 9 ($15, $19, $25, $29…). A line can set its own `markup`. `category` is the shop filter, in this order. Edit and push: the workflow creates/updates the products and commits lib/merch-catalog.json plus the mockups.",
